    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-476" contextRef="c-25">&lt;div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: 1em"&gt;NOTE A - ORGANIZATION, OPERATIONS AND BASIS OF PRESENTATION:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: 1em"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Organization&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs Pipeline, L.L.C. (&amp;quot;White Cliffs&amp;quot;) is a Delaware limited liability company formed on January 26, 2007.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt; White Cliffs is a joint venture owned 54.33% by ET CC Holdings, L.L.C., an indirect wholly-owned subsidiary of Energy Transfer LP (&amp;quot;Energy Transfer&amp;quot;), 35.67% by Plains Pipeline, LP, and 10% by Anadarko Wattenberg Company, LLC c/o Western Midstream Partners, LP.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;. White Cliffs is principally engaged in the transportation of crude oil and natural gas liquids (&amp;quot;NGLs&amp;quot;).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt; White Cliffs' operations and reporting are divided into the following pipeline systems:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline"&gt;Crude Oil Pipeline System&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs provides crude oil transportation services on approximately 527 miles of 12-inch diameter common carrier trunk pipelines that originate in Platteville, Colorado and terminate at a storage facility in Cushing, Oklahoma. This crude pipeline system connects the DJ Basin to the Cushing, Oklahoma market.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; text-decoration: underline"&gt;NGL Pipeline System.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs established NGL service from Platteville, Colorado to Cushing, Oklahoma on pipeline facilities parallel to the White Cliffs Crude Oil Pipeline system.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Regulation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;. White Cliffs' crude oil and NGL transportation activities are subject to regulation by the Federal Energy Regulatory Commission (&amp;quot;FERC&amp;quot;) and various state authorities. Regulatory bodies exercise statutory authority over matters such as rates, underlying accounting practices, and rate-making agreements with customers.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Presentation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The financial statements presented herein are prepared in accordance with the accounting requirements of the FERC, as set forth in the applicable Uniform System of Accounts and published accounting releases, which constitute a comprehensive basis of accounting other than accounting principles generally accepted in the United States of America (&amp;quot;GAAP&amp;quot;). The most significant differences between GAAP and the financial statements presented herein are: (1) classification of certain accounts on the balance sheet, statement of income and the statement of cash flows and (2) use of FERC approved depreciation rates.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 13.2pt; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE B - SUMMARY OF SIGNIFICANT ACCOUNTING POLICIES AND OTHER MATTERS:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Use of Estimates&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The preparation of financial statements requires management to make estimates and assumptions that affect the reported amounts of assets and liabilities and disclosure of contingent assets and liabilities at the date of the financial statements and the reported amounts of revenues and expenses during the reporting period.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Actual results could differ from those estimates.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Cash and Cash Equivalents&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Cash equivalents consist of highly liquid investments, which are readily convertible into cash and have original maturities of three months or less.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The cash deposits and temporary cash investments are placed with high credit quality financial institutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;At times, White Cliffs' cash and cash equivalents may be uninsured or in deposit accounts that exceed the Federal Deposit Insurance Corporation insurance limit.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Property, Plant and Equipment&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs capitalizes expenditures related to property, plant and equipment that have a useful life greater than one year for (1) assets purchased or constructed; (2) existing assets that are replaced or improved; or (3) land regardless of cost.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;During construction, White Cliffs capitalizes direct costs, such as labor, materials and overhead.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs records property, plant and equipment at its original cost. Depreciation is computed on a composite straight-line method at rates based on the expected economic lives of the various classes of assets.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Accounts Receivable and Allowance for Credit Losses&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 4.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Accounts receivable are carried at the amount owed by customers less an allowance for credit losses, if deemed necessary.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs evaluates the collectability of accounts receivable based on review of a specific customer's ability to meet its financial obligation or as a result of changes in the overall aging of accounts receivable.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;White Cliffs' allowance for credit losses was not material as of December 31, 2025 and 2024.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 22.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Contract Balances with Customers&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs satisfies its obligations by transferring goods or services in exchange for consideration from customers.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The timing of performance may differ from the timing that the associated consideration is received from the customer, thus resulting in the recognition of a contract liability.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs recognizes a contract liability if the customer's payment of consideration precedes White Cliffs' fulfillment of the performance obligations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Certain contracts contain provisions requiring customers to pay a fixed fee for a right to use White Cliffs' assets, but allow customers to apply such fees against services to be provided at a future point in time.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;These amounts are reflected as deferred revenue until the customer applies the deficiency fees to services provided or becomes unable to use the fees as payment for future services due to expiration of the contractual period the fees can be applied or physical inability of the customer to utilize the fees due to capacity constraints.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;Performance Obligations&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;At contract inception, White Cliffs assesses the goods and services promised in its contracts with customers and identifies a performance obligation for each promise to transfer a good or service that is distinct.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Revenue is recognized when (or as) the performance obligations are satisfied, that is, when the customer obtains control of the good or service.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs generally does not own the crude oil that it transports or stores.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 4.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs is a limited liability company that has elected to be treated as a partnership for income tax purposes.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Accordingly, the tax effects of White Cliffs' activities generally accrue to its members.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-left: 4.5pt; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Environmental Remediation&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs accrues environmental remediation costs for work at identified sites where an assessment has indicated that cleanup costs are probable and reasonably estimable. Such accruals are undiscounted and are based on currently available information, estimated timing of remedial actions and related inflation assumptions, existing technology and presently enacted laws and regulations. If a range of probable environmental cleanup costs exists for an identified site, the minimum of the range is accrued unless some other point or points in the range are more likely, in which case the most likely amount in this range is accrued.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE C - COMMITMENT AND CONTINGENCIES:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; text-align: justify"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;White Cliffs may be subject to various legal proceedings and claims that arise in the ordinary course of business. In the opinion of management, the amount of any ultimate liability with respect to any such actions will not materially affect the company's financial position or results of operations. &lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE D - RELATED PARTY TRANSACTIONS:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; text-decoration: underline; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;Operating Management Fees&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold; letter-spacing: -0.1pt"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2; font-size: 12pt"&gt; 				&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt"&gt;White Cliffs pays ET CC Holdings, LLC an annual fixed operating fee as reimbursement for providing certain services including business development, legal services, accounting and financial reporting, human resource services, and other as defined in the&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="line-height: 115%; font-family: Arial; font-size: 10pt"&gt;operating agreement. The fixed operating fee is escalated annually by five percent and is ET CC Holdings, LLC 's sole reimbursement and compensation for any allocation of ET CC Holdings, LLC 's or its affiliates' overhead related to the services. &lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;The fixed operating fee amounted to $0.76 million and $0.73 million for the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024, respectively.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE E - REGULATORY MATTERS:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;In accordance with the Order Denying Rehearing, Denying Petition and Granting Remedies in Docket No. RM20-14-004 (&amp;quot;Order&amp;quot;) issued on November 20, 2025 footnote 111, we have determined that rebillings, as permitted in that Order, are not distortive. In accordance with the rebillings, $1 million has been included in operating revenues in the accompanying income statement for the year ended December 31, 2025.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial; font-weight: bold"&gt;NOTE F - SUPPLEMENTAL CASH FLOW INFORMATION:&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Arial"&gt;Accrued capital expenditures during the years ended December 31, 2025 and 2024 were $0.15 million and $0.6 million, respectively.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 0; line-height: 115%; widows: 2; orphans: 2"&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
